Graded view: its own Flags, unsure matches, Hodges-Lehmann PC Graded, earlier re-reads of busy grades

- Auth Pop / Auth Pop Higher removed (population needs Card Hedge Enterprise + a GemRate contract); layout
  versions v5 / v6 drop them from saved orders.
- PC Graded (last month) is the Hodges-Lehmann estimate (median of the Walsh averages) of last month's recorded
  sales of that grade and grader, else the chart value. CL stays Card Ladder's monthly average (the hover says so).
- pchist: a full graded table (30 sales) is re-read after 70% of its span, up to the normal 30-day refresh, so busy
  grades no longer lose sales before the next read.
- Rows the matcher left on "review" that Brett has not answered are tinted with an "unsure match" tag.
- The graded Flag is its own: the Flag column opens a reason menu (no longer opens Review); a "Flags (n)" button
  shows only the flagged rows; still filed in ids/marks.csv, never in the eBay Flags.
- Every word button's list and the Grading list have a search box and Select all / Deselect all.
- The line under the tabs describes the graded data in the graded and both views.
- Grading, the word buttons and Flags are hold-and-drag reorderable like the filter chips (saved in this browser).

